;; Rename the pair recall-count attributes from :stat/* to :recall/*, so the
;; recall-count model is named for the recall count, not for the /stats route
;; (ticket 24). The per-memory recall count already lives at :memory/recall-* and
;; needs no rename.
;;
;; Four :up steps:
;;   1. :schema/create the :recall/* attributes and the identity tuple.
;;   2. engram.migrations/copy-stat->recall copies each stored row's values onto
;;      the same entity, so the tuple rebuilds in place.
;;   3. engram.migrations/retract-stat-rows clears every :stat/* datom.
;;   4. :schema/remove the old tuple and the old :stat/* attributes.
;;
;; Step 3 exists because a direct :schema/remove of the components collides. The
;; tuple :stat/user+category+label stays unique while its components exist.
;; Removing one component makes Datalevin recompute the tuple for every row at
;; once, with that slot nil. Two rows that share a label but differ by user or
;; category then collapse to the same tuple value and break the unique
;; constraint. Step 3 instead retracts each row's components together as data, so
;; that row's tuple drops straight to all-nil and disappears, while the other
;; rows keep their distinct tuples. After step 3 the attributes hold no datoms,
;; so the step 4 removal succeeds.
;;
;; :transaction? false, so step 1 commits the new schema before step 2 reads it,
;; and before steps 3 and 4 drop the old data and attributes. This avoids a
;; mid-transaction schema-visibility quirk. :irreversible? true, because the copy
;; and the remove have no auto-inverse. The cron backup of the data directory is
;; the rollback path. No attribute is full-text, so the migration triggers no
;; re-index.
{:transaction? false
 :irreversible? true
 :up [{:schema/create {:recall/user     {:db/valueType :db.type/string}
                       :recall/category {:db/valueType :db.type/string}
                       :recall/label    {:db/valueType :db.type/string}
                       :recall/user+category+label {:db/tupleAttrs [:recall/user :recall/category :recall/label]
                                                    :db/unique :db.unique/identity}
                       :recall/lifetime {:db/valueType :db.type/long}
                       :recall/decayed  {:db/valueType :db.type/double}
                       :recall/last-recalled {:db/valueType :db.type/instant}}}
      engram.migrations/copy-stat->recall
      engram.migrations/retract-stat-rows
      {:schema/remove [:stat/user+category+label
                       :stat/user :stat/category :stat/label
                       :stat/lifetime :stat/decayed :stat/last-request]}]}
